  "description": "A multi-session EEG dataset of longitudinal two-class (left/right hand) motor imagery brain-computer interface training combined with transcutaneous spinal cord stimulation. It includes 27 participants, 25 able-bodied and 2 with spinal cord injury. EEG was recorded with 32 channels plus 3 EOG channels at 512 Hz during cue-based, offline motor imagery trials.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with an ANT Neuro eego amplifier using Ag/AgCl electrodes (10-20 montage, 512 Hz, CPz reference, AFz ground), with 32 EEG channels and 3 EOG channels. Participants performed cue-based, offline two-class motor imagery (left vs. right hand) trials of 4 s each, with transcutaneous spinal stimulation. Events were annotated using HED 8.4.0.",
